cted': 'Because 15 > series length (10), every index i returns original.getValue(0). No IndexOutOfBoundsException is thrown.', 'description': 'Check that a barCount larger than the series size safely returns the earliest value for all indices.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'barCount', 'value': 2147483647}], 'expected': 'For any index i, returnedIndicator.getValue(i) == original.getValue(0). The implementation must handle Integer.MAX_VALUE without overflow or exception.', 'description': 'Stress‑test the method with an extreme positive barCount to ensure robust handling of integer overflow scenarios.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'barCount', 'value': 0}], 'expected': 'The delegate of the returned NumericIndicator is an instance of PreviousValueIndicator whose internal offset is 0.', 'description': 'Confirm that even for barCount 0 the method wraps the original indicator with a PreviousValueIndicator (rather than returning the original object directly).'}]}, {'group': 'NumericIndicator.previous(int) - chaining behavior', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'barCount', 'value': 2}], 'expected': 'Let A = original.previous(2) and B = A.previous(3). For any index i >= 5, B.getValue(i) == original.getValue(i‑5). For i < 5 the fallback to the earliest value applies as defined by PreviousValueIndicator.', 'description': 'Verify that successive calls to previous() accumulate their offsets (2 + 3 = 5).'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'barCount', 'value': 5}], 'expected': 'original.previous(5) yields exactly the same values as the chained version original.previous(2).previous(3) for every index.', 'description': 'Ensure that a single call with the summed barCount is equivalent to multiple chained calls.'}]}, {'group': 'NumericIndicator.previous(int) - constant delegate behavior', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'barCount', 'value': 4}], 'expected': 'When the underlying delegate is a ConstantIndicator (always returns Num.valueOf(42)), the returned NumericIndicator also returns 42 for every index, regardless of barCount.', 'description': 'Confirm that previous() does not alter constant values and works correctly with a constant delegate.'}]}]
